me{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265950 1111 #uuid "bc6cf462-d1ff-5367-8640-e982e089afea" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265951 1034 "z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265951 1111 #uuid "80677a3e-179c-5307-8815-5716e23a8b1e" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265952 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265953 13194139533920 true] [17592186265952 1089 "q-107404" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265952 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533920 true] [17592186265952 1100 "Express $z=\\frac{1-\\text{i}}{4}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265952 1113 #uuid "6a55cea2-0632-5c86-ad59-90081e2751a2" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265952 1145 "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ We get\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{1-\\text{i}}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}+(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{1}{4}+(-\\frac{1}{4})\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{1}{4}$ is positive and $y=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative, $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{4})}{(\\frac{1}{4})}| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z=\\frac{1-\\text{i}}{4}$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))\n$$" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265954 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265955 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265956 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265957 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265958 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1041 "selection" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265954 13194139533920 true] [17592186265953 1110 #uuid "d5b8cd4e-2ca5-5f25-83bd-999a34e1c748" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265954 1034 "z=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265954 1111 #uuid "37fe3d7e-4b95-5d99-b141-cd7c35573b18" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265955 1034 "z=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265955 1111 #uuid "4e63922c-9952-5728-840a-ddb17d6091b1" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265956 1034 "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265956 1111 #uuid "c3176ea4-f443-50f2-8b30-b3818482e106" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265957 1034 "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265957 1111 #uuid "47635084-efa7-5caa-8f5a-79257e4932d1" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265958 1034 "z=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265958 1111 #uuid "eda9688d-579f-5fa8-85b7-ca355922a5c6" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265959 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265960 13194139533920 true] [17592186265959 1089 "q-107504" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265959 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533920 true] [17592186265959 1100 "Express $z=-\\frac{2}{3\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265959 1113 #uuid "c0791cfa-321a-5888-9413-89be1eb2fcca" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265959 1145 "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $-3\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{2}{3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(-3\\text{i})}{(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\text{i}}{-9{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\text{i}}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}=0+\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i},$ the magnitude is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=0$  and $y=\\frac{2}{3}$ is positive, $z$ lies on the positive direction of the $y$-axis. So,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\n$$" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265961 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265962 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265963 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265964 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265965 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1041 "selection" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265961 13194139533920 true] [17592186265960 1110 #uuid "6e588cbb-f092-53bf-8fa5-011809180929" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265961 1034 "z=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265961 1111 #uuid "79662cb1-82d2-5532-aa08-286b903c8ddf" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265962 1034 "z=\\frac{4}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265962 1111 #uuid "c42f919a-0c91-5215-8bfb-970af4dd5aa7" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265963 1034 "z=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533920 true] [17592186265963 1111 #uuid "df65c59e-9e0d-50e5-a29f-22ee643f6a97" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265964 1034 "z=\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" 13194139533920 true] [17592186265964 110